    "turn_text": "Well, yeah, we had a hearing on the committee last week on this. Actually, it was just a pause by the administration. It wasn't a executive order. It wasn't a piece of legislation passed. It was just a directive. to the agency. It's interesting people think that these projects can just start and stop like this and these are multi-year projects that need to be planned for years in advance and I think a pause on this is misguided. Plus we have plenty of natural gas that we can export to help our friends and allies in Europe who are looking west for American gas after the invasion of Ukraine by Vladimir Putin and then if you Think about lowering climate emissions globally. We can do that through cleaner burning US-produced natural gas. Why should our allies or why should even Vietnam or even China buy gas from Russia or from Iran? They can buy it from us and we can produce",
